# Every path. The CSP only reports for now: violations go to Sentry's security endpoint and nothing
# is blocked. Workers get it from their script's response, so it covers every path. connect-src must
# list every API in src/deployments.ts (deployments.spec.ts checks). Installed apps keep the headers
# their service worker cached until it updates, so an enforced policy can't be loosened quickly.
#
# The other headers are enforced. X-Frame-Options blocks framing while frame-ancestors only reports.
# no-referrer is safe because Sentry and tRPC use CORS fetches, which still send Origin (and Sentry
# sets its own referrerPolicy). COOP is safe because the app neither opens popups nor needs its
# opener. Permissions-Policy turns off features Flock doesn't use; WebAuthn and clipboard-write keep
# their default of 'self'.
